{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778616036901,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"functions.read:32","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/src/ontology/run.sh","limit":50},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/src/ontology/run.sh</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/bin/sh\n2: # Wrapper script for docker.\n3: #\n4: # This is used primarily for wrapping the GNU Make workflow.\n5: # Instead of typing \"make TARGET\", type \"./run.sh make TARGET\".\n6: # This will run the make workflow within a docker container.\n7: #\n8: # The assumption is that you are working in the src/ontology folder;\n9: # we therefore map the whole repo (../..) to a docker volume.\n10: #\n11: # See README-editors.md for more details.\n12: \n13: MEMORY_GB=${MEMORY_GB:-8}\n14: IMAGE=${IMAGE:-odkfull:v1.6}\n15: MEMORY_JAVA=\"-Xmx${MEMORY_GB}G\"\n16: ODK_DEBUG=${ODK_DEBUG:-no}\n17: \n18: docker pull obolibrary/$IMAGE\n19: \n20: echo \"Running ODK with ${MEMORY_GB} GB of memory, using ${IMAGE}.\"\n21: \n22: TIMECMD=\n23: if [ x$ODK_DEBUG = xyes ]; then\n24:     # If you wish to change the format string, take care of using\n25:     # non-breaking spaces (U+00A0) instead of normal spaces, to\n26:     # prevent the shell from tokenizing the format string.\n27:     TIMECMD=\"/usr/bin/time -f ### DEBUG STATS ###\\nElapsed time: %E\\nPeak memory: %M kb\"\n28: fi\n29: \n30: docker run --memory=${MEMORY_GB}g  -v $PWD/../../:/work -w /work/src/ontology -e ROBOT_JAVA_ARGS=${MEMORY_JAVA} -e JAVA_OPTS=${MEMORY_JAVA} --rm -ti obolibrary/$IMAGE $TIMECMD \"$@\"\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/bin/sh\n# Wrapper script for docker.\n#\n# This is used primarily for wrapping the GNU Make workflow.\n# Instead of typing \"make TARGET\", type \"./run.sh make TARGET\".\n# This will run the make workflow within a docker container.\n#\n# The assumption is that you are working in the src/ontology folder;\n# we therefore map the whole repo (../..) to a docker volume.\n#\n# See README-editors.md for more details.\n\nMEMORY_GB=${MEMORY_GB:-8}\nIMAGE=${IMAGE:-odkfull:v1.6}\nMEMORY_JAVA=\"-Xmx${MEMORY_GB}G\"\nODK_DEBUG=${ODK_DEBUG:-no}\n\ndocker pull obolibrary/$IMAGE\n\necho \"Running ODK with ${MEMORY_GB} GB of memory, using ${IMAGE}.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/run.sh","time":{"start":1778616036894,"end":1778616036900}},"id":"prt_e1dc6eb71001JVrg3qia4EwQWE","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","messageID":"msg_e1dc6d10f001yk9J91JcA92DeG"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1778616036941,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"id":"prt_e1dc6ee4c001E0Odxc0Tnq3RwV","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"e8f14588fabcdfb7edb4a98162697019acd95815","messageID":"msg_e1dc6d10f001yk9J91JcA92DeG","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":49861,"input":41,"output":92,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":49728}},"cost":0.0104088}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1778616038413,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"id":"prt_e1dc6f40b001fjUFwJZyOn7EsS","messageID":"msg_e1dc6ee70001vufGQbQ9ZhZTvC","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","snapshot":"e8f14588fabcdfb7edb4a98162697019acd95815","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778616053468,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"functions.skill:33","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"odk"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"odk\">\n# Skill: odk\n\n# Running ODK commands in this repo\n\n## TL;DR\n\n`src/ontology/run.sh` is the official wrapper, but it ends in `docker run -ti` so it **fails silently in any non-TTY context** (Claude Code, CI, non-interactive shells) with `the input device is not a TTY` and exits without running the command.\n\nIf you have a TTY, prefer `run.sh`. If you don't, call docker directly with `-i` only.\n\n## When you have a TTY (interactive terminal)\n\n```bash\ncd src/ontology && sh run.sh <command> <args...>\n```\n\nExamples:\n```bash\nsh run.sh make NORM\nsh run.sh owltools --use-catalog mondo-edit.obo --obsolete-replace MONDO:A MONDO:B -o -f obo mondo-edit.obo\nsh run.sh robot verify --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo --queries ../sparql/qc/general/qc-foo.sparql -O reports/\n```\n\n## When you don't have a TTY (Claude Code, CI, scripts)\n\nSymptom: `sh run.sh <anything>` prints `the input device is not a TTY` and exits with no further output, no file changes.\n\nWorkaround — invoke docker directly using the same image and mounts as `run.sh`, but with `-i` only:\n\n```bash\ndocker run --memory=8g \\\n  -v /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/REPO:/work \\\n  -w /work/src/ontology \\\n  -e ROBOT_JAVA_ARGS=-Xmx8G -e JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx8G \\\n  --rm -i obolibrary/odkfull:<TAG-FROM-RUN.SH> \\\n  <command> <args...>\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/REPO` = the repo root (the parent of `src/`).\n- `<TAG-FROM-RUN.SH>` = whatever tag is set in `IMAGE=` in `src/ontology/run.sh`. **Always read `run.sh` first to look up the current tag** — do not hardcode `v1.6` or any other version.\n\n## Reading the right image tag\n\nDon't memorize the version. The line in `run.sh` is the source of truth:\n\n```bash\ngrep '^IMAGE=' src/ontology/run.sh\n# IMAGE=${IMAGE:-odkfull:v1.6}\n```\n\n## Common ODK commands you'll need\n\n| What | Command body (after `run.sh` or after the `docker run ... -i obolibrary/odkfull:<TAG>` prefix) |\n|---|---|\n| Normalize edit file | `make NORM` then `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` (run from `src/ontology`) |\n| Convert / syntax check | `robot convert --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo` |\n| Run a QC query | `robot verify --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo --queries ../sparql/qc/general/qc-X.sparql -O reports/` |\n| Merge / obsolete with replacement | `owltools --use-catalog mondo-edit.obo --obsolete-replace MONDO:A MONDO:B -o -f obo mondo-edit.obo` |\n\n## Notes\n\n- All ODK commands assume CWD is `src/ontology/`.\n- `make NORM` writes to a file called `NORM` in `src/ontology/`. You must `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` afterward.\n- `robot verify` exits non-zero on QC failures and writes one TSV per failing query under `-O reports/`. Empty exit + `PASS Rule ... 0 violation(s)` = clean.\n- If `run.sh` reports `the input device is not a TTY`, do **not** retry the same command — it will keep failing. Switch to the docker-direct invocation.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.agents/skills/odk\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"odk","dir":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.agents/skills/odk","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: odk","time":{"start":1778616053453,"end":1778616053466}},"id":"prt_e1dc72ec7002bCFdys3H9sCx0E","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","messageID":"msg_e1dc6ee70001vufGQbQ9ZhZTvC"}}
