{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778616216806,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"functions.write:43","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","content":"Thank you for your patience. I have created the new term **preneoplastic lesion** (MONDO:7770012) as a child of **precancerous condition** (MONDO:0021074), per your clarification in this thread. The definition follows the refined version discussed here, and the term includes a tracker item linking back to this issue. This change will be included in the next release. Changes are committed in PR #<NN>.\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778616216798,"end":1778616216805}},"id":"prt_e1dc9a2a0001v0HSpMGZfP5gWs","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","messageID":"msg_e1dc954e9001BYk3jsBY8cvX5L"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778616226029,"sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"functions.write:44","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","content":"## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a new term **preneoplastic lesion** (MONDO:7770012) as requested in issue #9781.\n\n### Changes\n- Added new term `MONDO:7770012` with name **preneoplastic lesion**\n- Parent: `MONDO:0021074` (precancerous condition)\n- Definition: \"A precancerous condition characterized by accumulation of some molecular alterations necessary for malignant transformation in a clonal proliferation of cells, representing an intermediate stage in carcinogenesis with increased risk of progression to invasive neoplasia.\"\n- Definition references: PMID:37775701, PMID:39754221, PMID:40624726, PMID:40684183\n- Added term tracker item linking back to issue #9781\n\n### Rationale\nDuring discussion in issue #9781, it was initially proposed that \"preneoplastic lesion\" be added as an exact synonym of \"precancerous condition\". However, the requestor correctly clarified that this would be inappropriate because conditions such as \"clonal hematopoiesis of indeterminate potential\" are precancerous but not preneoplastic lesions. The requestor subsequently confirmed that \"preneoplastic lesion\" should be created as a **new child term** of `precancerous condition` (MONDO:0021074), rather than of `pre-malignant neoplasm` (MONDO:0000611), since preneoplastic lesions represent a biological stage *before* neoplasm formation.\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] Read and analyzed the full issue discussion carefully\n- [x] Checked existing terms \"precancerous condition\" and \"pre-malignant neoplasm\" in the ontology\n- [x] Verified next available new-term ID (MONDO:7770012)\n- [x] Created term with appropriate parent, definition, and citation sources\n- [x] Ran `make NORM` to normalize OBO serialization\n- [x] Ran `robot convert` syntax validation (passed with no errors)\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778616226022,"end":1778616226027}},"id":"prt_e1dc9ace0001iwLWFeu9Nz6HYY","sessionID":"ses_1e240ce6affeHxZw7mlsDfwBUG","messageID":"msg_e1dc954e9001BYk3jsBY8cvX5L"}}
